BCL `for_each` clauses map to element iteration patterns in the Revit API. The `for_each` tells the compliance checker to evaluate the rule independently for each matching element.

**Pattern:**
```
BCL for_each: item in collection
  -> Revit: foreach (Element item in FilteredElementCollector...)
```

**Implementation for the NO EXIT sign rule:**
```csharp
public static List<string> CheckNoExitSigns(Document doc)
{
    List<string> results = new List<string>();

    // BCL: for_each: opening in building.openings
    // Revit: collect all doors (openings)
    var doors = new FilteredElementCollector(doc)
        .OfCategory(BuiltInCategory.OST_Doors)
        .WhereElementIsNotElementType()
        .ToElements();

    // BCL: where: not is_exit(opening)
    // Revit: filter to non-exit doors
    var nonExitDoors = new List<FamilyInstance>();
    foreach (Element elem in doors)
    {
        FamilyInstance door = elem as FamilyInstance;
        if (door == null) continue;

        Parameter egressParam = door.LookupParameter("Is Egress");
        bool isEgress = egressParam != null && egressParam.AsInteger() == 1;
        if (!isEgress)
            nonExitDoors.Add(door);
    }

    // BCL: count(confusion_factors.true) >= 2
    // Evaluate confusion factors for each non-exit door
    foreach (FamilyInstance door in nonExitDoors)
    {
        int confusionCount = 0;

        // Factor 1: looks like an exit (outward swing)
        if (door.FacingFlipped || !door.HandFlipped)
            confusionCount++;

        // Factor 2: near an exit path
        Parameter nearExitParam = door.LookupParameter("Near Exit Path");
        if (nearExitParam != null && nearExitParam.AsInteger() == 1)
            confusionCount++;

        // Factor 3: prominent location
        Parameter visibleParam = door.LookupParameter("High Visibility");
        if (visibleParam != null && visibleParam.AsInteger() == 1)
            confusionCount++;

        // BCL: where condition
        if (confusionCount < 2)
        {
            results.Add($"Door {door.Id}: Not confusable ({confusionCount} factors) - N/A");
            continue;
        }

        // BCL: must: sign(opening) exists with correct properties
        // Check for nearby NO EXIT sign
        bool hasNoExitSign = CheckForNoExitSign(doc, door);

        results.Add($"Door {door.Id}: {confusionCount} confusion factors - " +
                    $"{(hasNoExitSign ? "PASS" : "FAIL: Needs NO EXIT sign")}");
    }

    return results;
}
```

**General BCL for_each to Revit patterns:**
| BCL for_each | Revit Implementation |
|---|---|
| for_each: door in building.doors | FilteredElementCollector(OST_Doors).foreach |
| for_each: room in building.rooms | FilteredElementCollector(OST_Rooms).foreach |
| for_each: stair in building.stairs | FilteredElementCollector(OST_Stairs).foreach |
| for_each: pipe in system.pipes | PipingSystem.PipingNetwork iteration |
| for_each: floor in building.floors | FilteredElementCollector(OST_Floors).foreach |

The key principle: BCL `for_each` becomes a collector + loop, and each element is independently evaluated against the `where` filter and `must` constraints.

