BCL conditional logic maps directly to C# if/else if/else chains or dictionary lookups in the Revit API. Here are two implementation patterns:

**Pattern 1: Direct if/elif mapping**
```csharp
public static (bool compliant, string detail) CheckBurialDepth(
    Element conduit, Document doc)
{
    // Get wiring method from element type or parameter
    string typeName = conduit.Name.ToLower();
    Parameter methodParam = conduit.LookupParameter("Wiring Method");
    string method = methodParam?.AsString()?.ToLower() ?? typeName;

    // Get actual burial depth
    Parameter depthParam = conduit.LookupParameter("Burial Depth");
    double depthInches = (depthParam?.AsDouble() ?? 0) * 12.0;

    // BCL conditional logic -> C# if/else if
    double requiredInches;
    if (method.Contains("direct_burial") || method.Contains("direct burial"))
    {
        requiredInches = 24.0;
    }
    else if (method.Contains("rigid_metal") || method.Contains("rigid metal") || method.Contains("rmc"))
    {
        requiredInches = 6.0;
    }
    else if (method.Contains("rigid_pvc") || method.Contains("pvc") || method.Contains("schedule 80"))
    {
        requiredInches = 18.0;
    }
    else
    {
        requiredInches = 24.0; // Default to most conservative
    }

    bool compliant = depthInches >= requiredInches;
    return (compliant, $"Depth={depthInches:F1}in, Required={requiredInches}in ({method})");
}
```

**Pattern 2: Dictionary lookup (preferred for many conditions)**
```csharp
// Map BCL conditionals to a requirements dictionary
Dictionary<string, double> depthRequirements = new Dictionary<string, double>
{
    { "direct_burial", 24.0 },
    { "rigid_metal", 6.0 },
    { "rigid_pvc", 18.0 },
    { "emt", 18.0 },
    { "intermediate_metal", 18.0 }
};

// Find matching requirement
double required = 24.0; // default
foreach (var kvp in depthRequirements)
{
    if (method.Contains(kvp.Key))
    {
        required = kvp.Value;
        break;
    }
}
```

**Dynamo Python equivalent:**
```python
depth_requirements = {
    "direct_burial": 24.0,
    "rigid_metal": 6.0,
    "rigid_pvc": 18.0
}

required = 24.0  # default
for key, value in depth_requirements.items():
    if key in method:
        required = value
        break
```

The dictionary pattern is cleaner and easier to maintain when BCL rules have many conditional branches, such as pipe sizing tables or occupancy-based fixture counts.

